    categoryZh: "电影布光与光影氛围",
    description: "A bright, even lighting style with minimal shadows that creates an optimistic, clean, or ethereal atmosphere, common in comedies, commercials, and dream sequences. The classic Hollywood musical relied on high-key lighting — Vincente Minnelli's \"An American in Paris\" and \"The Band Wagon\" glow with uniform brightness. Kubrick used clinical high-key lighting in the space station sequences of \"2001\" to create sterile futurism, and Sofia Coppola bathes \"Marie Antoinette\" in high-key pastel light to capture the candy-colored excess of Versailles. The technique is also fundamental to the visual language of romantic comedies from Nora Ephron to Nancy Meyers.",
    promptTemplate: "High-key lighting flooding [Subject] in bright even illumination with barely a shadow to be found, the overall exposure pushed a third of a stop hot to create an airy blown-out feeling, shot on Alexa at 1280 ISO with Cooke S7 glass for gentle halation around the highlights, the dreamy overlit aesthetic of warmth without shadows, optimism without darkness",
